      $('#demo-explanation').innerHTML=`<div><h3>Accepted is a result. Preview is a view.</h3><p>Coverage, spacing and cleanup can reject requested candidates. Display budgets can then show less of the accepted planting without changing that result. Hiding the preview is not a render-disable switch.</p></div><div><h3>Final output needs a source mesh.</h3><p>Automatic final render prepares the accepted model output. A Point placeholder has no source mesh to render. Original materials, maps and renderer qualification are separate checks; these markers prove none of them.</p></div>`;
